## Coding Rules

- Use strict TypeScript for frontend code and typed Python for backend code.
- Follow existing Next.js App Router patterns for UI and proxy routes.
- Validate Python API and agent data with Pydantic.
- Python is authoritative for backend schemas; expose OpenAPI and derive TypeScript client types.
- All agents call the Python provider adapter, never a provider SDK directly.
- Agent outputs are structured and Pydantic-validated.
- Keep orchestration deterministic: code owns routing, retries, stopping conditions, and state updates.
- Keep eval cases and graders provider-neutral so the same suite runs against Ollama, hosted APIs, and vLLM.
- Show confidence levels and evidence citations on every claim.
- Never claim omniscience — expose uncertainty.
- Never say "best candidate" — say "gap coverage" (factual).
- Use shadcn/ui components. Light mode only.
- Design: Linear + Vercel + Stripe aesthetic. Minimal, professional.
- Keep the demo path fast, stable, and easy to present live.
- Run frontend and Python verification after meaningful changes.

## Do NOT Build

- Digital twin / fine-tuning / LoRA
- GRPO / RL training
- Dark mode
- Complex video avatar (LivePortrait, voice cloning)
- Full Jira/GitHub OAuth integration
- Admin settings / user accounts
- Knowledge graph 3D visualization (optional, cut if time-tight)
